  { title: 'The ranges move.', text: `"These addresses are updated regularly", so an allow rule that isn't refreshed falls behind ${cite(5)}.` },
  { title: 'Bot Fight Mode stays on.', text: `On Cloudflare, "Bot Fight Mode can't be skipped with WAF custom rules" ${cite(5)}.` },
];

const AHEAD = [
  { title: 'You have a buyer from the day you sign.', text: `Perplexity is the buyer. The Financial Times reported "around $200 million in annual revenue" (via ${a(X.gigazine, 'Gigazine')}, published 2026-02-19). A Perplexity executive told it the service has "more than 100 million users", the vendor's own figure. On FORA, any agent your terms allow can buy from your Exchange.` },
  { title: 'Joining asks only for crawler rules.', text: `Joining is an email and a contract, and the technical ask Perplexity documents is the crawler rules above. How a partner's paywall lets a subscriber in isn't documented. FORA asks you to publish a file that names your Exchanges, sign with an Exchange, set your terms in its console and install its edge function on your CDN (${a('/getting-started/what-is-fora/', 'What is FORA?')}). From then on, the edge function decides on each request whether an AI bot gets the page.` },
  { title: 'It counts traffic FORA can\'t see.', text: `Two of Comet Plus's counts, human visits and agent actions, happen in the reader's browser, as Digiday describes them. Perplexity's position is that "Your AI assistant must be indistinguishable from you" (${a(X.bullying, 'Bullying is not innovation')}, published 2025-11-04). FORA's edge function knows AI bots by the names they send, and a request it doesn't recognize passes as a reader. It can't charge a browser that doesn't identify itself, and Comet Plus counts that traffic inside Perplexity.` },
  { title: 'Its share counts citations.', text: `Search citations are one of its three counts. FORA fixes the charge when the agent buys, and a usage report "never re-prices a purchase" (${a('/protocol/licensing-terms/#metering-modes', 'Licensing terms')}). A FORA usage report can record that an answer cited you, but that doesn't change the charge, and no FORA pricing unit counts citations.` },
  { title: 'It sends paying readers to your own site.', text: `Comet Plus "is specifically designed to allow publishers to own the direct relationship with their audience" ${cite(2)}. FORA has no reader product. It licenses machine access.` },
  { title: 'The pool is a set sum, if it still pays.', text: `Publishing executives told Digiday the model "does seem more developed than the ad revenue share program … mostly because the company is setting aside a specific pool of money" (${a(X.hurdles, 'Digiday')}, published 2025-08-28). Whether Comet Plus still pays out isn't public. On FORA, your income is the sum of what agents buy, with no floor.` },
];

