---
<LandingLayout
  title="Perplexity Comet Plus, and FORA — FORA resources"
  description="How Perplexity says Comet Plus pays publishers from its subscription revenue, where the program stands, what it asks of your site, where it is ahead of FORA, and how a publisher can run both on one site."
>
  <AudienceHero
    current="resources"
    badge={`Resources · ${a('/resources/content-marketplaces/', 'Content marketplaces')} · Perplexity`}
    title="Perplexity says Comet Plus pays the publishers it signs. <em>With FORA, any AI company can buy at your price.</em>"
    sub="Comet Plus is Perplexity's own program. It shares subscription revenue with the publishers Perplexity signs, by how Perplexity's products use their sites. FORA lets any AI agent buy each access at the price you set, and records each sale."
    updated={resourceUpdated(HREF)}
  >
    <a href="#ahead" class="btn btn-primary">Where Perplexity is ahead</a>
    <a href="#together" class="btn btn-ghost">Run both</a>
  </AudienceHero>

  <Band tone="near" id="glance" label="At a glance" title="Perplexity and FORA, side by side" lead="The facts a revenue team and an engineering lead act on.">
    <GlanceCard vendor="Perplexity Comet Plus" groups={GLANCE} />
  </Band>

  <Band label="The short answer" title="Perplexity buys for itself. FORA lets any agent buy.">
    <CardGrid items={SHORT_ANSWER} />
    <Callout kind="define" {...DEFINITIONS.exchange} />
  </Band>

  <Band tone="light" label="How Comet Plus is meant to pay you" title="From a subscriber's payment to your share, in seven steps" lead="Comet is Perplexity's browser, and Comet Assistant is its AI helper. Comet Plus is the subscription whose revenue Perplexity shares with the publishers it signs. As Perplexity describes it:">
    <Split aside="1.45fr">
      <Figure
        src={`${IMG}/perplexity-1.png`}
        title="How Comet Plus is built to pay, as Perplexity describes it."
        alt="Subscribers pay for Comet Plus ($5, or included in Pro and Max); the subscription revenue becomes a pool, minus a small portion for compute, which Perplexity splits, a share each, among the publishers it signs, by weights per partner that are not public, over human visits, search citations and agent actions counted in its own products. The statement format is not public."
      />
      <StepList slot="aside" items={PAY_STEPS} />
    </Split>
  </Band>

  <Band tone="near" compact label="Comet Plus in four numbers">
    <KeyFacts items={KEY_FACTS} />
  </Band>

  <Band id="paid-so-far" label="Who has been paid so far" title="Perplexity names its partners. No publisher has confirmed a Comet Plus payment.">
    <PullQuote
      quote="Real cash payments starting immediately, and obviously set to grow every month as our Pro and Max subscribers increase."
      who="Jessica Chan, Perplexity, on Comet Plus, to Digiday in August 2025"
      source="How Perplexity's new revenue model works, according to its head of publisher partnerships"
      href={X.digiday}
    />
    <p class="prose" set:html={`Perplexity names its partners, from TIME and Der Spiegel in 2024 to Condé Nast, Le Monde and The Washington Post as Comet Plus launch partners (${a(X.partners, 'launch partners')}). No count of Comet Plus participants or subscribers is published. No publisher has confirmed a Comet Plus payment in any source found. The 2024 ad share is in the <a href="#background">background</a> at the end of the page.`} />
  </Band>

  <Band tone="light" label="What it takes on your site" title="Crawler rules, and an open question about your paywall" lead={`No partner integration guide was found as of 2026-11-15. Perplexity's technical guidance for site owners is its ${a(X.crawlers, 'crawler page')} and its ${a(X.robots, 'robots.txt help article')}. Perplexity's docs ask for no DNS change and no code on your CDN. Two things aren't documented: which user agent Comet sends, and how your paywall lets a Comet Plus subscriber in.`}>
    <Split aside="380px">
      <Callout kind="engineers" collapse="Show the five points" points={ENGINEERS} />
      <Figure
        slot="aside"
        src={`${IMG}/perplexity-2.png`}
        title="Three ways Perplexity reaches your pages, and where you decide."
        alt="Your robots.txt stands apart from the request path: it is honored by the bot, not enforced. PerplexityBot, the search crawler, follows it (a change may take up to 24 hours), Perplexity-User generally ignores it, and Comet's user agent isn't documented. On the request path, your CDN firewall lets PerplexityBot in by an allow rule matching its user agent and IP ranges, and the FORA edge function refuses it by default, a list you can change; your firewall is where you stop Perplexity-User, and the edge refuses it without a signed link; Comet's user agent isn't documented, and it passes the edge as a reader."
      />
    </Split>
    <Callout kind="define" {...DEFINITIONS.edgeFunction} />
  </Band>

  <Band tone="near" label="What can go wrong" title="In Perplexity's own docs">
    <Callout kind="caution" points={CAUTIONS}>
      <PullQuote
        small
        quote="[Perplexity-User] generally ignores robots.txt rules."
        who="Perplexity, on the crawler that fetches for a user"
        source="Perplexity Crawlers"
        href={X.crawlers}
      />
    </Callout>
    <Callout kind="search" id="search-traffic" text={SEARCH_FORA.text} links={SEARCH_FORA.links}>
      <p>PerplexityBot builds Perplexity's search index, and it follows robots.txt. How refusing it changes your Comet Plus share isn't public.</p>
    </Callout>
  </Band>

  <Band id="ahead" label="Where Perplexity is ahead" title="What Perplexity does that FORA doesn't">
    <PointList items={AHEAD} />
  </Band>

  <Band tone="light" label="The differences, question by question" title="Eight questions a publisher asks of any licensing deal" lead="Perplexity runs one buyer's licensing program, and FORA is a protocol for many buyers and sellers. The first four rows compare things Perplexity doesn't set out to do for other AI companies. On the last four, Perplexity is ahead on a set pool and a smaller documented ask of your site. FORA is ahead on setting your own price and on a signed record per sale.">
    <Callout kind="define" {...DEFINITIONS.broker} />
    <div class="table-gap"><CompareTable vendor="Perplexity Comet Plus" rows={COMPARE} /></div>
    <p class="prose">The two compete for how you license Perplexity's use of your content. They compose on your site, where you choose what each Perplexity crawler gets.</p>
  </Band>

  <Band tone="near" id="together" label="How FORA works with Perplexity" title="Both on one site today">
    <h3 class="sub-h">Works today <StatusTag status="live" /></h3>
    <PointList items={WORKS_TODAY} />
    <h3 class="sub-h">Doesn't fit</h3>
    <p class="prose" set:html={`<b>Comet Plus as a marketplace for FORA agents.</b> A FORA Broker presents offers that a seller signs. Perplexity licenses no partner's article to other AI companies. Its Search API sells results that its terms say are "sourced from the public internet", and the customer doesn't own them (${a(X.searchApi, 'Search API terms')}). There is no signed license offer to present.`} />
    <p class="prose" set:html={'<b>Paying FORA sales through Comet Plus.</b> Perplexity offers no payment service to anyone else (none found as of 2026-11-14). It allocates the pool from its own traffic counts.'} />
  </Band>

  <Band label="What to do" title="If you're in Comet Plus, or weighing it">
